The World Economic Forum's Future of Jobs Report 2023 estimates that 44% of workers' core skills will be disrupted within 5 years, requiring continuous upskilling.
Adults who engage in formal learning after age 25 earn 10–15% more over their careers than those who stop, according to OECD earnings data across 30 countries.
Amazon's Career Choice programme (pre-paying employees for education in high-demand fields) has a 90% job placement rate and measurably reduced turnover — making lifelong learning a business investment, not just a personal one.
